* How this library was assembled:

This library is assembled out of a subset of source files from libarchive
(only what's necessary to create .tar.gz archives) and libz (only what's
necessary to compress as required by libarchive). Most files are unmodified
with a few exceptions (see .orig files).

The two libraries share the config.h file that is pre-generated by the
autoconf module (see instructions below on how to update it). libz's zconf.h
(copy of zconf.h.in) is patched to #include this file at the beginning.

* Updating static config.h file:

rm config.h # Important!

sed -re 's/(HAVE_[A-Z_0-9]+)/\n\1\n/g' *.c *.h | \
  sed -nre 's/^(HAVE_[A-Z_0-9]+)$/#undef \1/p' | \
  sort -u >config.h.in
# Manually remove HAVE_CONFIG_H, HAVE_XXX, HAVE_MAJOR, HAVE_DECL_UINT64_MIN,
# HAVE_WAITPID, HAVE_UTIMENSAT, HAVE_FUTIMENS
# Manually add MAJOR_IN_SYSMACROS, SIZEOF_INT, SIZEOF_LONG
# Manually add `#undef ssize_t`.
# Manually add:

#ifdef _WIN32
#  ifndef __MINGW32__
typedef int pid_t;
typedef unsigned short mode_t;
#  endif
typedef short uid_t;
typedef short gid_t;
#endif

# Manually add HAVE_STDARG_H (for zlib, see zconf.h.in)
# Manually remove HAVE_HIDDEN, HAVE_MEMCPY, HAVE_VSNPRINTF (zlib)

# Uncomment config.h generation in buildfile.
b h{config} # Copy over from out dir.
# Comment config.h generation in buildfile.

Note: if updating to a newer version of libarchive/libz, diff *.h.in files
for any new checks that do not start with HAVE_.